ck" content="true" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:android:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:ios:url" content="meetup://" data-next-head=""/><meta property="al:web:url" content="https://www.meetup.com/" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:site" content="@meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:image" content="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/shared/meetup-flyer.png" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:description" content="Find Meetup events and groups so you can do more of what matters to you and meet people near you who share your interests." data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:iphone" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:iphone" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:ipad" content="375990038" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:ipad" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:id:googleplay" content="com.meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta property="twitter:app:name:googleplay" content="Meetup" data-next-head=""/><meta name="robots" content="noindex, follow" data-next-head=""/><link rel="canonical" href="https://www.meetup.com/find/" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://secure-content.meetupstatic.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preconnect" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><link rel="dns-prefetch" href="https://www.googletagmanager.com" data-next-head=""/><script type="application/ld+json" data-next-head="">[{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Pickering - Practical Philosophy Meetup 🇨🇦","url":"https://www.meetup.com/practical-philosophy-club-ontario/events/316787631/","description":"**🏛️ WHAT'S PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY ABOUT?**\n\nPractical Philosophy is a weekly meet-up that brings critical thinkers together for an opportunity to dive deep on a topic, practice communicating, and building a community. All with no ‘official’ philosophy knowledge required! 😎\n\nPractical Philosophy is based on the idea that philosophy should be accessible to all, and not something reserved only for academics. Each week we choose a topic, and the goal is to use the conversation to develop our critical thinking and communication as we explore that topic.\nThe goal is to help develop our Critical Thinking, Communication, and Community 🙌\n\n**📓 HOW DOES IT WORK?**\n\nEach week, we pick one topic and discuss it. The topic for the week is shared, generally in the [Whatsapp group](https://tally.so/r/WORMLP), along with jump-off points to get the conversation going.\n\nWhen groups get bigger than 7-8 people, it’s important that we break into smaller groups. This way we are able to maintain a conversational flow as opposed to having our meetups feel like a discourse or lecture.\n\n**General Meeting Agenda**\nEach Practical Philosophy meet-up follows this general timeline:\n\n* 19:00-19:15 - People arrive and chat, get to know each other before the official start.\n* 19:15-19:25 - Meeting introduction, explanation of Practical Philosophy and the topic for the week, read the guidelines and the overview so attendees know what to expect in terms of timelines.\n* 19:25-20:45 - Break into small groups - introduce yourselves and general thoughts on the topic, open discussion afterwards. At this point the group can review the ‘jump-off’ questions as needed, but they are just there to help guide the conversation. It’s not obligatory to answer them.\n* 20:45-21:00 - Bring everyone back together to discuss conclusions of the topic - each group gives a short 1-minute summary. Organizer concludes the meeting and everyone takes a group photo.\n* 21:00 - The official meeting is over but it’s a great opportunity to get to know people in a non-structured environment, so we often stick around, chat, and get to know each other.\n\n**🧧PRICING?**\n\nPractical Philosophy is operated entirely on voluntary donations! If we are meeting in a café, buy a beverage! Donations are 100% voluntary, but they help us to bring the gift of deep conversation to people around the world. If you'd like to support, you can [donate here](https://www.zeffy.com/en-CA/donation-form/donate-to-practical-philosophy)!\n(Practical Philosophy is a registered Canadian charity)\n\n**💛 WHAT PEOPLE SAY ABOUT PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY**\n\n**🗣** “I feel like Philosophy Club helps someone build their own belief system through a series of perspectives while not promoting what’s right and wrong” - Ekam\n\n🗣 “I got hooked from day 1 (the topic was authority) and felt it was the right place for me. I feel it is a place where people can go to learn and discuss new perspectives and increase critical thinking and community by interacting with people who might challenge your point of views but at the same time encourage you to have openness and mind flexibility.” - Daniel\n\n**🤓 FAQ**\n\n* **Do I need to study or read anything to attend?**\n\nNo preparation is necessary. This isn’t a study of other thinkers. We want to know what you think about the topic, not what an old philosopher thought. If you have a perspective from a religion or a school of thought to share, throw it on the table and we’ll discuss it.\n\n* **Is there a specific philosophy that Practical Philosophy is focused on?**\n\nThe goal of our meet-ups is to not have dogmatic discussions, and flex our critical thinking muscles. Because of this, we want to hear from every realm of thought, and don't study a particular school.\n\n* **Is it mostly men that attend?**\n\nSurprisingly, no! Although often, philosophy is seen as a Candelabra affair in a dark room with a bunch of guys, our Practical Philosophy meetups are generally 50/50 between genders, and we don’t meet in any dark rooms.\n\n* **Can I come alone?**\n\nOf course you can, we encourage it :)\n\n* **Can I be late?**\n\nPlease don't be! We do have a 15 minute grace period where we allow people to funnel in while we hang out, but after that if you arrive too late, it disrupts the flow of the conversation.\n\n* **Where do you meet?**\n\nThe location is posted in Meetup and our [Whatsapp](https://tally.so/r/WORMLP) group for this location. It is HIGHLY RECOMMENDED that you join the Whatsapp group! If you want to know what other cities have a Practical Philosophy Club, you can see our chapters on our [website](https://www.practicalphilosophy.club/).\n\n🤝**POLICY**\n\nTo respect our members privacy, we ask that no one privately message a member without first getting explicit consent. (This looks like speaking in person and being asked to message privately.) Contacting or texting other participants without prior consent is not permitted and may result in removal from the group. Practical Philosophy reserves the right to enforce this policy at its discretion to maintain a safe and respectful environment.\n\n**PRACTICAL PHILOSOPHY CLUB - Philosophy, everywhere. ✨**\n\nWe started in Practical Philosophy back in 2021 and there are now 50+ chapters in 25+ countries, including Canada, Spain, Japan, Mexico and many more! 🗺️\n**\\*\\*\\***\n**Join our [Pickering Whatsapp](https://tally.so/r/WORMLP) 👈**\n**Follow us on [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/practicalphilosophyclub/) 👈**\n**Our [website](https://www.practicalphilosophy.club/) 👈**","startDate":"2026-10-20T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"The Shops at Pickering City Center","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Pickering","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"1355 Kingston Road, Pickering, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Practical Philosophy Club - Ontario 🇨🇦","url":"https://www.meetup.com/practical-philosophy-club-ontario/"},"performer":"Practical Philosophy Club - Ontario 🇨🇦"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Customer Segmentation: Who Will Pay for Your Product?","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-public-library-small-business-networking-meetup/events/316714369/","description":"The fastest way to start a new business is to try to sell it to everybody. This session will teach you to narrow down your target group by using geography, demographics, and behavioral statistics to determine demand. It will also cover how to spot your early adopters, i.e., the people who need what you're building most will be flexible while you get it right. We'll discover how to narrow down your target audience, and how to determine if you were well informed in your decisions.\n\nThe program includes a short networking component, providing participants with an opportunity to connect with other entrepreneurs.\n\nPresented by Ryan Knight, TPL's 2026 [Entrepreneur in Residence](https://tpl.ca/programs-and-classes/featured/entrepreneur-in-residence/) (EIR) at Toronto Reference Library.\n\n**Registration via TPL website:** [https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31](https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/6a99b901d94765189bb97c31)\n**Drop-ins welcome until room capacity is reached.**\n\nAccessibility\nLive or automated closed captioning, sign language interpretation, intervenor services, or attendant services are available upon request. Please submit your request at least 2 weeks in advance to: [tpl.ca/accessibility-events](https://tpl.ca/accessibility/accessibility-supports/programs-and-events/?_gl=1*v83hy7*_ga*NDk5MDg2NTE1LjE3NjYwMDgxODQ.*_ga_G99DMMNG39*czE3NjkxMDY3NDMkbzE0JGcxJHQxNzY5MTA2ODM0JGozOCRsMCRoMA..).","startDate":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Toronto Public Library - Toronto Reference Library","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"789 Yonge St, Toronto, ON M4W 2G8, Canada, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Public Library Small Business Networking Meetup","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-public-library-small-business-networking-meetup/"},"performer":"Toronto Public Library Small Business Networking Meetup"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"October's Book: Weyward","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto_bookclub/events/316401720/","description":"2019: Under cover of darkness, Kate flees London for ramshackle Weyward Cottage, inherited from a great aunt she barely remembers. With its tumbling ivy and overgrown garden, the cottage is worlds away from the abusive partner who tormented Kate. But she begins to suspect that her great aunt had a secret. One that lurks in the bones of the cottage, hidden ever since the witch-hunts of the 17th century.\n\n1619: Altha is awaiting trial for the murder of a local farmer who was stampeded to death by his herd. As a girl, Altha’s mother taught her their magic, a kind not rooted in spell casting but in a deep knowledge of the natural world. But unusual women have always been deemed dangerous, and as the evidence for witchcraft is set out against Altha, she knows it will take all of her powers to maintain her freedom.\n\n1942: As World War II rages, Violet is trapped in her family's grand, crumbling estate. Straitjacketed by societal convention, she longs for the robust education her brother receives––and for her mother, long deceased, who was rumored to have gone mad before her death. The only traces Violet has of her are a locket bearing the initial W and the word weyward scratched into the baseboard of her bedroom.\n\nWeaving together the stories of three extraordinary women across five centuries, Emilia Hart's Weyward is an enthralling novel of female resilience and the transformative power of the natural world.","startDate":"2026-10-20T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Duke of York","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"39 Prince Arthur Ave, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Ladies Book Club","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto_bookclub/"},"performer":"Toronto Ladies Book Club"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"🎱 learn to play pool 🎱 FREE for ladies 🎱make new friends (Junction) 🎱","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontobilliardsclub/events/316672297/","description":"🎱**TBC Tuesday Socials at Shoxs**🎉\n\nEnjoy a night of getting out of the house, meeting new people, and enjoying a relaxed night of pool with **Toronto Billiards Club** at **Shoxs**.\n\nThis Tuesday evening social is all about **good vibes, community, and accessible pool**. Whether you are brand new to the game or have years of experience, you will feel comfortable here.\n\n**What to expect:**\n✅ friendly, inclusive, and welcoming social atmosphere\n✅ beginners welcome\n✅ instruction and guidance from TBC hosts\n✅ casual pool games, conversation, drinks, and food\n✅ no pressure, no leagues, no egos\n\nif you have ever thought *“I want to play pool but don’t know where to start”* or *“I don’t want to walk into a pool hall by myself”* this event is made for you. many of our regulars first showed up solo.\n\n💬 **First time attending?**\nOur hosts will introduce you, help you get a game going, and make sure you are comfortable throughout the night.\n\n💵 **Event Fee:**\n$20 per person\n**Payable by cash or e-transfer (dean@tbcpool.org)**\nPlease contact the event organizer if you have payment questions\n\n📋 **House Rules:**\nAll attendees are expected to follow TBC Meetup Rules during the event. If you have questions about rules, fees, or the format, feel free to message an organizer.\n\n👉 **Call to action:**\nBring a friend or come solo. show up curious. Leave with new connections and more confidence at the table.\n\nSee you Tuesday and welcome to the TBC community!\n\n**TBC Admin**","startDate":"2026-10-20T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Shoxs","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"2827 Dundas St. W., Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Billiards Club 🎱","url":"https://www.meetup.com/torontobilliardsclub/"},"performer":"Toronto Billiards Club 🎱"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto Urban Playground Parkour Fundamentals","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-urban-playground-parkour-basics-crew/events/316673224/","description":"If you have ever watched someone navigate a park bench or a concrete ledge and thought that looks like fun, this session is for you. We are getting together at the park to break down the fundamentals of parkour in a way that is accessible and straightforward. Whether you are completely new to movement or just want to brush up on your landings, rolls, and basic vaults, we keep the focus on building confidence and control in a supportive environment.\n\nExpect to spend the time moving at your own pace while we work through some drills together. We prioritize safety and technical understanding over flashy tricks, so you do not need to be an athlete to join in. Just bring comfortable shoes, some water, and an open mind. If you have been looking for a reason to get outside and explore the city through a different lens, we would love to have you join us. Please let us know if you can make it by clicking the RSVP button so we know how many people to expect.\n\nSpots are limited and registration is required. Please register at the link below to hold yours.\n\n[Click To Save Your Spot](https://remoteready.io/neo_registration?event_title=Toronto%20Urban%20Playground%20Parkour%20Fundamentals&src=the-urban-playground-parkour-basics-crew)","startDate":"2026-10-20T14:30:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-5-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"HHGF+3P Toronto","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"HHGF+3P Toronto, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"The Urban Playground Parkour Basics Crew","url":"https://www.meetup.com/the-urban-playground-parkour-basics-crew/"},"performer":"The Urban Playground Parkour Basics Crew"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"ROM Tuesday Night group walking tour & Dinner after (optional)","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tamclub/events/316722854/","description":"### 🏛️ ROM Museum Evening Visit & Social\n\n📅 **Tuesday**\n⏰ **6PM**\n📍 **Royal Ontario Museum (ROM), Toronto**\n\nJoin us for a relaxed evening exploring the **Royal Ontario Museum** and connecting with new people in a casual, social setting. We’ll meet at the entrance and head inside together to explore select exhibits at our own pace—perfect for art, history, culture, and science lovers.\n\nThis event is ideal if you:\n\n* Enjoy museums and cultural experiences\n* Want to meet new people in a low-pressure setting\n* Prefer small-group, meaningful conversations\n\n**Event Plan**\n\n* 6:00 PM – Meet inside the ROM ground floor (Near the Large Dinosaur)\n* 6:15 PM – Explore the museum together\n* 7:30 PM – Optional food or snacks nearby\n\n**Important Notes**\n\n* Free Museum admission ticket is **included** in the meetup event fee. *(You must provide your contact to the host for the Free ticket OR obtain your own free ticket from ROM website)*\n* Please arrive on time so we can enter together. If you are late, you can text or call the Host to find the group.\n\n✨ Come curious, come friendly, and enjoy a cultural night out in Toronto!\n\n**Event Fee\\***\n\n* $3.99\n\n**Payment**\n**Cash** \\- In person when you arrive at event\n**Etransfer** [themoja@outlook.com](themoja@outlook.com) (use password **meetup**)\n**Credit Card** - *[pay via stripe](https://buy.stripe.com/00w5kD1dac4SaUk1hT0oM01)*\n\n**Exhibits:**\n\\- 1st Floor \\- Special exhibit\\, China\\, Korea and First People\n\\- 2nd Floor \\- Dinosaurs\\, Birds\\, Bio\\-diversity\\, Rocks\\, Natural World\n\\- 3rd Floor \\- History & Being Legendary exhibit\n\\- 4th Floor \\- Wildlife Photography of the Year\n\n💬 **Stay Connected:**\n***Join Whatsapp Group - [CLICK HERE](https://docs.google.com/forms/d/e/1FAIpQLSflzD3fDrU5sLARAT5yDF3OhEu3Vj-2P7ci8mP5FYX46rt1NQ/viewform)***\n***Follow on Instagram - [CLICK HERE](https://www.instagram.com/tam.club/)***\n\n*\\*We may charge a small fee to help cover platform costs and to make sure people who sign up are committed to attending. It also helps us keep hosting more quality events in the future.*","startDate":"2026-10-20T22:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Royal Ontario Museum","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"100 Queens Park, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto Asian Meetup - TAM","url":"https://www.meetup.com/tamclub/"},"performer":"Toronto Asian Meetup - TAM"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Tantric Family Constellation: Temple of Love & Money","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316787682/","description":"**TANTRIC FAMILY CONSTELLATIONS**\n**Tantric Temple Mysteries**\n\n**This is the project overview only.**\n**Themes and dates may change.**\n\n**To find the exact topic, date and register, please join:**\n\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**About this event**\n\n**Tantric Family Constellations is a group practice combining Archetypal / Family Constellations with a living tantric Temple space.**\n\n**Each meeting has its own theme.**\n\n**For example:**\n\n**Love & Money • Ancient Languages of Love • Love & Loneliness • Masculine & Feminine • Desire & Freedom • Relationship Patterns**\n\n**The theme gives us a field to explore — but every participant discovers their own personal story inside it.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 1 — Discover your pattern**\n\n**We begin by exploring different dimensions of the evening’s theme together.**\n\n**Then each participant goes through a mini-constellation to see their own pattern, model or hidden dynamic.**\n\n**Instead of only thinking about the question, you can see how its different forces are arranged for you:**\n\n**What attracts you?**\n**What do you avoid?**\n**Where does your energy stop?**\n**What are you moving toward?**\n\n**This creates a personal map for the second part of the evening.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Part 2 — Enter the Temple**\n\n**Then we open the Tantric Temple.**\n\n**The constellation points become living centers in the space.**\n\n**Participants are free to move between them, following their own inner process.**\n\n**You may stay with one energy, move toward another, step away, return, observe what happens in your body, or allow yourself to gradually absorb a quality that previously felt distant.**\n\n**At the same time, you encounter other participants moving through their own paths.**\n\n**Through presence, movement and consensual interaction, the personal constellation becomes a living group field.**\n\n**There is no fixed choreography and no need to perform.**\n\n**You follow your own rhythm.**\n\n**The practice is about allowing yourself to experience, embody and integrate the different energies of the constellation rather than only understand them intellectually.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**Why “Temple”?**\n\n**The Temple is a temporary tantric space where symbolic and archetypal energies can be experienced through the body, movement and connection with others.**\n\n**The journey is individual, but it happens inside a shared field.**\n\n**You may discover that a quality which looked abstract during the constellation becomes much more understandable once you can actually move toward it, stay with it and experience it in contact with others.**\n\n**⸻**\n\n**No previous constellation or tantra experience is required.**\n\n**Participation is voluntary, and you can always choose your own level of involvement and contact.**\n\n**The space is based on:**\n\n**consent • respect • confidentiality • personal boundaries • freedom of movement**\n\n**This is a transpersonal personal-growth practice.**\n\n**Details, themes, dates and registration:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**\n\n**TICKETS**\n\n1. **Regular Ticket — $100 CAD**\n1. **Early Bird Ticket — $65 CAD**\n**If you register and pay before August 31.**\n**3. Supportive Ticket — $55 CAD**\n**For people with limited financial resources.**\n**4. Bring a Friend — $150 CAD for 2 people**\n\n**If the price is too much for you, send a personal message on Telegram: t.me/AndyTherapist to ask about volunteer options.**\n\n**HOW TO PAY**\n\n**Send an Interac e-Transfer to:**\n**andy.litvinov@gmail.com**\n**After payment, send a screenshot of the confirmation to: t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Please mention which event you are registering for.**\n\n**After registration, you will be added to the participants’ group.**\n\n**If you have any questions, feel free to message:**\n**t.me/AndyTherapist**\n**Toronto Tantra community:**\n**t.me/TorontoTantra**","startDate":"2026-10-20T23:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/events/316786142/","description":"MASSAGE CLUB & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY\nThis is the project overview only!\nDates might change.\n\nTo find the exact dates and register for the event, please join our Telegram group:\n\nT.me/TorontoTantra\nT.me/AndyTherapist\n\nMASSAGE & BODY PSYCHOTHERAPY CLUB\n\nHave you ever explored massage not only as relaxation, but also as a way to reconnect with your body, emotions, and nervous system?\n\nIn Toronto there are many massage services, but not many spaces where people can safely learn, practice and exchange conscious touch together.\n\nWe would like to create such a club.\n\nA warm, respectful space for people interested in massage, bodywork, somatic practices and body-oriented psychotherapy.\n\nYou don’t need professional massage experience. Beginners are welcome.\n\nJoin our group and leave a message if you would like to be added to the waiting list.\nt.me/TorontoTantra\n\nAbout this event\n\n• What is the Massage & Body Psychotherapy Club?\n\nIt is a practice evening where we explore conscious touch, relaxation, massage techniques and simple body-oriented therapeutic exercises.\n\nThe purpose is not only to relax muscles, but also to develop better contact with your body, reduce stress and learn how safe touch can support emotional regulation and connection.\n\n• What will we be doing?\n\nDepending on the evening, we may explore:\n\n- simple relaxation massage techniques\n- conscious touch and body awareness\n- grounding and nervous-system regulation\n- breathing and relaxation exercises\n- somatic and body-psychotherapy exercises\n- practicing giving and receiving\n- communication of boundaries and consent\n\nPractices can be done in pairs or small groups and will be guided step by step.\n\n• Massage exchange\n\nOne of the main parts of the club is a structured massage exchange.\n\nYou can experience both sides:\ngiving touch and receiving touch.\n\nThe goal is not to perform a “perfect massage,” but to become more sensitive to another person’s body, learn to listen through your hands, communicate clearly and discover what kind of touch feels supportive.\n\nImportant terms & agreements\n\nConsent first: every exercise and every touch is optional.\n\nRespect boundaries: you can say yes, no, stop, slower, softer or change the practice at any moment.\n\nKeep it therapeutic: this is a bodywork and personal-development space, not a sexual service or dating event.\n\nStay present: no alcohol or recreational drugs during the event.\n\nConfidentiality: personal experiences shared during the practice stay within the group.\n\nThe club may be interesting for people curious about:\n\nmassage • bodywork • somatic therapy • body-oriented psychotherapy • conscious touch • nervous-system regulation • relaxation • tantra-inspired body awareness\n\nDetails, dates and registration:\nt.me/TorontoTantra","startDate":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"","addressRegion":"","addressCountry":""}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-tantra-circle/"},"performer":"T.me/TorontoTantra Circle"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Free ESL Practice and Support","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-mbglenao/events/316779750/","description":"The Church of St. Timothy is excited to offer support to newcomers in Canada. Our goal is to provide conversational language practice through informal instruction and feedback in a welcoming and diverse community. All levels welcome!\n\nWe invite all new-comers, English language students, visitors to Canada, parents of children temporarily attending schools in Toronto, international university students, and anyone looking to enhance their language skills.\nWe aim to build community where friendships can flourish, in order to help participants establish meaningful connections, learn about life in Toronto, and access practical resources as you settle in to this new city and country.\n\nWe begin every Tuesday at 10:00 a.m. with time to socialize. Our formal program begins at 10:30 a.m.\nEach week we will have different activities and topics, including practicing English conversation, reading short articles, learning about common pronunciation and grammar mistakes, etc.\nOur volunteers would love to get to know you and offer gentle and constructive feedback to help you improve your English!","startDate":"2026-10-20T14:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-2-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"100 Old Orchard Grove","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"100 Old Orchard Grove, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Church of St. Timothy, North Toronto Meetup Group","url":"https://www.meetup.com/meetup-group-mbglenao/"},"performer":"Church of St. Timothy, North Toronto Meetup Group"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Toronto Midtown - MDI Men's Team","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gta-mens-teams-meetings/events/316788680/","description":"We are a group of men that meet weekly. Regular attendees do not always RSVP but we usually have 12 men present. Expect a frank and confidential space where you can speak personally, engage in interesting conversations or get support for your personal goals.\n\n**We start our meeting at 7:15 sharp. You can rsvp via meetup or email Saul (sauljoy@gmail.com) for this week’s address.**\n\nGuests are welcome but it's pretty casual so make sure you are expected in case we move outdoors to the park.\n\nOur group is part of Mentor Discover Inspire (MDI)\nThe MDI Mission: To cause greatness by mentoring men to live with excellence and, as mature masculine leaders, create successful families, careers and communities.\nFrom MDI website: https://goo.gl/3DQ6aY\nFrom Toronto Star: [https://goo.gl/oDH3uX](https://goo.gl/oDH3uX)","startDate":"2026-10-20T23:15:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Queens Park","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Toronto","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"Queen's Park Cresent, Toronto, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Toronto & York Region Men's Circles - MDI","url":"https://www.meetup.com/toronto-gta-mens-teams-meetings/"},"performer":"Toronto & York Region Men's Circles - MDI"},{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"Event","name":"Le French Meetup avec Angélique - 3 $","url":"https://www.meetup.com/le-french-meetup-avec-angelique/events/316363169/","description":"Chers ami(e)s,\n\nJe pense que cela serait bien de mettre en place un abonnement annuel au Meetup: 36 dollars pour 12 mois de Meetup par personne à partir d'avril 2025. Comme ça, je pourrai continuer à utiliser le site Meetup pour nos rencontres mensuelles. Pour ceux qui ne viennent que quelques fois par an, je les ferai payer 3 dollars à chaque fois. Je vous demanderai lors de notre prochaine rencontre de me payer en espèce ou par transfert interac à angelfirouzi@gmail.com la somme de 36 dollars.\n\nMerci\nAngélique\n\nDear friends,\n\nI think it would be a good idea to put in place a yearly subscription to our Meetup: 36 dollars for 12 months of Meetup starting this month of April 2025. Like this I will be able to use the Meetup website for our monthly meetings. For those who come once in a while, I will make them pay 3 dollars each time. I will ask you at our next meeting to pay me 36 dollars in cash or by Interac transfer to angelfirouzi@gmail.com.\n\nThank you,\nAngélique\n\nHi All,\n\nAre you looking to speak and excel in your French? The French Meetup with Angélique meets all your expectations. Join us the third Wednesday of every month at 5 pm. This is a great opportunity to meet in a francophone setting, converse in French and socialize in a friendly and instructive environment.\nThere is a 3 dollar fee per person for each meetup to cover the annual fee of the meetup.com website. There is also a requirement to consume a minimum of 1 item per person.\nLooking forward to meeting you.\nAngélique\n\nBonjour à toutes et à tous,\nVous voulez parler ou pratiquer votre français? Le French Meetup avec Angélique vous donne cette occasion de discuter en français et socialiser dans une bonne ambiance amicale, amusante et instructive, tous les troisième mercredis du mois à 17h. L’esprit de convivialité que je propose nous permettra à toutes et à tous de nous reposer tout en ayant une notion de français. Je compte sur vous!\nUne participation de 3 dollars par session et par personne pour payer les frais annuels du site Meetup.com ainsi qu’un minimum d’une consommation sont requises.\nAu plaisir de vous voir bientôt.\nAngélique","startDate":"2026-10-20T21:00:00.000Z","endDate":"","eventStatus":"https://schema.org/EventScheduled","image":"/images/fallbacks/redesign/group-cover-4-square.webp","eventAttendanceMode":"https://schema.org/OfflineEventAttendanceMode","location":{"@type":"Place","name":"Cream n Sugar Cafe and Bistro","address":{"@type":"PostalAddress","addressLocality":"Richmond Hill","addressRegion":"ON","addressCountry":"ca","streetAddress":"8910 Yonge St, Richmond Hill, ON"}},"organizer":{"@type":"Organization","name":"Le French Meetup avec Angélique","url":"https://www.meetup.com/le-french-meetup-avec-angelique/"},"performer":"Le French Meetup avec Angélique"}]</script><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/2/d/f/9/highres_528071769.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/6/b/6/3/highres_536307491.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/d/1/5/0/highres_535973584.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/photos/event/c/e/d/2/highres_536272946.jpeg" as="image" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" as="image" imageSrcSet="https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/fallbacks/redesign/event-cover-1.webp?w=640 1x, https://secure.meetupstatic.com/next/images/fallbacks/redesign/event-cover-1.webp?w=828 2x" data-next-head=""/><link rel="preload" href="https://secure.mee